        "title": "California Advance Directive — Advance Health Care Directive",
        "custodian": {
          "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
          "display": "Carewish (patient-held document)"
        },
        "section": [
          {
            "title": "Healthcare Agent",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "code": "81335-2",
                  "display": "Patient Healthcare agent"
                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>I choose the following person as my agent to make health care decisions for me:</p><p>Daniel Torres · (559) 555-0142 · daniel@example.com</p><p>If my agent is not willing, able, or reasonably available to act, I choose:</p><p>Lucía Torres · (559) 555-0199</p><p>My agent may make all health care decisions for me that I could make myself, guided by the instructions in this document and my other known wishes. This includes choosing, refusing, or stopping any care, treatment, service, or procedure.</p><p>My agent may also decide to withhold or withdraw life-sustaining treatment, including artificial nutrition and hydration, even if doing so may allow me to die.</p><p>My agent&#39;s authority begins when my doctor determines that I am unable to make my own health care decisions.</p></div>"
            },
            "entry": [
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                "display": "Daniel Torres"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
                "display": "Lucía Torres"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Personal Care Experience",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "code": "81338-6",
                  "display": "Patient Goals, Preferences, and Priorities for Care Experience"
                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>What matters most to me:</p><ul><li>Being able to recognize and talk with my family</li><li>Being at home</li><li>Music &lt;3 &amp; &quot;quiet&quot; mornings</li></ul><p>About my faith, culture, and traditions:</p><p>Please call Father José at St. John parish.</p><p>Other instructions:</p><p>I would like my dog Pepper to visit.</p></div>"
            },
            "entry": [
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000017"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000018"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Preferences Under Certain Health Conditions",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "code": "81336-0",
                  "display": "Patient Goals, preferences, and priorities under certain health conditions"
                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>If I have an incurable and irreversible condition that will result in my death within a relatively short time:</p><p>I do not want my life to be prolonged by life-sustaining treatment. I want care that keeps me comfortable.</p><p>If I become unconscious and, to a reasonable degree of medical certainty, I will not regain consciousness:</p><p>I do not want my life to be prolonged by life-sustaining treatment. I want care that keeps me comfortable.</p><p>If I have an end-stage or irreversible condition, such as advanced dementia, and can no longer recognize my loved ones or care for myself:</p><p>I want my agent to decide, with my doctors, based on my values and wishes.</p><p>Artificial nutrition and hydration (food and fluids through a tube or IV):</p><p>I want a trial period of artificial nutrition and hydration, to be stopped if it is not helping me recover.</p><p>Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR):</p><p>I do not want CPR if I am in any of the conditions described above.</p><p>Relief from pain:</p><p>I want treatment for pain and discomfort at all times, even if it may hasten my death.</p></div>"
            },
            "entry": [
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011"
              },
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Upon Death",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "code": "81337-8",
                  "display": "Patient Goals, Preferences, and Priorities Upon Death"
                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>Donation of organs, tissues, and body parts at my death:</p><p>I give any needed organs, tissues, or parts.</p></div>"
            },
            "entry": [
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Witnesses and Notary",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "code": "81339-4",
                  "display": "Witness and Notary Document"
                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>Advance Health Care Directive (Cal. Prob. Code § 4701)</p><p>Print Advance Health Care Directive. Don&#39;t sign it yet.</p><p>Sign in front of 2 adult witnesses (age 18 or older) or a notary public. Either one works.</p><p>Choose witnesses who meet California&#39;s rules.</p><p>None of your witnesses can be:</p><ul><li>Your agent or alternate agent</li><li>A health care provider who is treating you</li><li>An employee of your doctor or health care provider</li><li>An owner or operator of a hospital, nursing home, or care home where you are a patient or resident</li><li>An employee of a hospital, nursing home, or care home where you are a patient or resident</li></ul><p>At least one of your witnesses must not be:</p><ul><li>Related to you by blood, marriage, or adoption</li><li>Someone who would inherit from you, under your will or by law</li></ul><p>Your witnesses sign right after you, in front of you and each other.</p><p>Bring a photo ID. The notary needs to see it.</p><p>If you live in a skilled nursing facility, a patient advocate or ombudsman must also sign as a witness, even if you use a notary.</p></div>"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
